VORTEX third-party agent attribution
====================================

VORTEX does not vendor these projects. Adapters only probe for a local
executable and never fabricate a successful consult.

- CAI — https://github.com/aliasrobotics/cai — MIT
- Nebula — https://github.com/BerylliumSec/nebula — BSD-2-Clause
- PentestGPT — https://github.com/GreyDGL/PentestGPT — MIT
- HexStrike — https://github.com/0x4m4/hexstrike-ai — MIT (verify upstream before install)
- Strix — https://github.com/usestrix/strix — Apache-2.0
- PentAGI — https://github.com/vxcontrol/pentagi — MIT
- HackerAI, HALO, DarkMoon — no uniquely verified public local CLI is configured

Do not copy proprietary code into VORTEX. Install agents only with operator
approval and respect each project's license and trademark terms.

The observe → typed action → host-state reward loop in `backend/episode.py`
is conceptually informed by Windows Agent Arena's POMDP task framing
(https://github.com/microsoft/WindowsAgentArena, MIT). No WAA source is
vendored; VORTEX executes reviewed Linux argv only.
